    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38597" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπελ-ευστικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>coming on</i> or <i>to, touching on</i> a thing:
			hence, of casual mention, Eust.ad <i><span class="en">
				D.P.
				<u>Prooem.</u>
				p.69B.
			</span></i>
			Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eust.
					1440.18
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				7.26
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>of the nature of</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπέλευσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					2
				</span></i>
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κίνησις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Chrysipp.Stoic.
					2.282
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>occurring casually,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἶδος ἐν τοῖς λόγοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					12.3.27
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>liable to prosecution,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				POxy.
				1120.10
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A. D.)</span>.</div>
